F2 [Nit] review-c: the accepted mill state rests on a hand edit to a generated
file. scenes/maps/mill.ts line 1 says "GENERATED by scripts/design-mill.mjs -
edit the generator, not this file", but the rework changed the watermill line in
mill.ts and left scripts/design-mill.mjs unchanged, so a future generator run
silently drops the fix. plan.md line 81 allows the direct edit, rework-mill.json
line 5 records the change text, and green-p3.log lines 73-74 disclose the
divergence. The risk is durability, not a contract break. Nonblocking.

No blocking findings. Both Nits route to the plan or record owner at Phase 4
